<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP oil output up, gas output slips.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP oil output up, gas output slips.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd said on Tuesday its oil and condensate production for November increased to six million barrels compared with a year ago.</p>
<p>The rise was due to higher output from the Liverpool Bay and Bruce fields in the United Kingdom, the Griffin and Wanaea/Cossack fields in Australia and Kutubu in Papua New Guinea, BHP said.</p>
<p>These increases were partly offset by lower production from Australian fields including Bass Strait and the Timor Sea.  </p>
<p>Divestment of oil producing assets in North and South America lead to a lower contribution fromt those regions, BHP said.</p>
<p>Gas production slipped as higher U.K. gas production was offset by lower U.S. gas sales due to asset sales, it said.  </p>
